@startuml
title OmniDesk Sprint Workflow

start

:Review Product Goal / relevant milestone context;
:Review prioritized Product Backlog;
:Refine Product Backlog as needed;
:Perform Sprint Planning;
note right
Select sufficiently refined
Product Backlog items.
end note

:Define Sprint Goal;
:Confirm acceptance criteria and applicable Definition of Done;
:Confirm fixed/defined Sprint timebox;
:Break selected items into engineering tasks;
:Start Sprint;

partition "Sprint Execution" {
  :Perform lifecycle work required by the Sprint Goal;
  note right
  Requirements
  Analysis
  Design
  Implementation
  Testing
  Documentation

  Only the activities needed
  for the Sprint Goal are performed.
  end note

  :Run relevant automated and manual verification;
  :Run applicable quality and security checks;
}

:Timebox ends;
:Perform Sprint Review;
note right
Review the Increment and evaluate
the Sprint Goal using Done work.
Sprint Goal achievement does not
extend the Sprint timebox.
end note

if (Selected work item satisfies acceptance criteria and applicable DoD?) then (yes)
  :Record completed work as part of the Sprint Increment;
  note right
  A Sprint produces a meaningful,
  reviewable Increment.

  A Sprint does not automatically
  create a release.
  end note
else (no)
  :Record incomplete work and discoveries;
  :Return incomplete/discovered work to the Product Backlog for reassessment;
  note right
  Incomplete work is not
  automatically assigned
  to the next Sprint.
  end note
endif

:Record resulting decisions, discoveries, and backlog adaptations;

note right
Key principles:
- Sprint != SDLC phase
- Sprint != Milestone
- Sprint != Release
- Sprint closes when its timebox ends.
- Incomplete work returns to the Product Backlog.
- Future Sprint selection occurs
  through Sprint Planning.
end note

stop

@enduml
